CHAPTER V
PREVENTION AND HANDLING
Article 9
(1) The Local Government is obligated to organize the Prevention of Violence against Women in a swift, coordinated and integrated manner.
(2) The organization of Prevention of acts of Violence against Women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out through the fields of:
a. Education;
b. Public facilities and infrastructure;
c. Government and institutional governance
d. Economy and employment;
e. Social welfare;
f. Culture;
g. Information technology;
h. Religion; and
i. Family

REGENT OF PENAJAM PASER UTARA,

Considering that acts of violence against women constitute:

a. violations of human rights and therefore their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature without discrimination;

b. that to prevent and address violence against women, legal protection needs to be provided for women victims of violence;

c. that Penajam Paser Utara Regency does not yet have a regulatory basis regarding the implementation of protection for women victims of violence;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women Victims of Violence;

Article 10
Handling of women victims of violence is through the provision of integrated and coordinated services covering:

a. coverage of Women Victims of Violence who receive complaint handling by trained officers in the Integrated Service Unit;

b. coverage of Women Victims of Violence who receive health services by trained health personnel at community health centers and in hospitals;

c. coverage of Social Rehabilitation services provided by trained Social Rehabilitation officers for Women Victims of Violence in the Integrated Service Unit;

d. coverage of spiritual guidance services provided by trained spiritual guidance officers for Women Victims of Violence in the Integrated Service Unit;

e. coverage of law enforcement from the investigation level up to court decisions on cases of Violence Against Women;

f. coverage of Women Victims of Violence who receive Legal Aid services;

g. coverage of return services for Women Victims of Violence; and

h. coverage of Social Reintegration services for Women Victims of Violence.
-7-

Article 2
Protection of Female Victims aims to: a. protect Women Victims of Violence;
b. provide Services to Women Victims of acts of Violence; and c. empowerment of Women Victims of Violence;
d. capacity building of Women victims of violence in women's empowerment through related Regional Apparatus Organizations, Private Parties, Business World and others.

Article 8
(1) UPID PPA has the duty to carry out technical operational activities in its working area in providing services for women and children who experience problems of violence, discrimination, special protection, and other problems.
(2) UPTD PPA in carrying out its duties as referred to in paragraph (1) performs service functions:
a. public complaints;
b. victim outreach;
c. case management;
d. temporary shelter;
e. mediation; and
f. victim assistance.
(3) UPTD PPA in carrying out functions as referred to in paragraph (2) is conducted for basic services in 1 (one) Regency.
