CHAPTER II
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 3
Victims have the right to obtain:
a. Protection from:
1. Family;
2. police;
3. prosecutor's office;
4. court;
5. advocate; and
6. social institutions, or other parties either temporarily or based on a Protection order determination from the court.
b. Health services in accordance with medical needs;
c. special handling related to the confidentiality of Victims;
d. assistance by social workers and Legal Aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
e. Spiritual guidance services; and
f. Victims have the right to determine their own decisions related to which options will be implemented.

Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
1. Law Number 7 of 2002 concerning the Establishment of Penajam Paser Utara Regency in East Kalimantan Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2001 Number 20, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4182);
2. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95);
3. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times, most recently by Law Number 11 of 2020 concerning Job Creation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2020 Number 245, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6573);
4. Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 4 of 2018 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment of Regional Technical Implementation Units for the Protection of Women and Children (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2018 Number 532);

With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF PENAJAM PASER UTARA REGENCY and

